id: energy-charge
name: Energy Charge
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerBaseTier: 2
charge: true
exploitable: All adjacent Opponents
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Charge up your energy into a single, high-power attack.
text: >
  Energy Charge Maneuver: Charge up your energy into a single, high-power attack.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –KP Cost: 2(bT)
  –Exploitable: All adjacent Opponents.
  –Effect: Declare an Attacking Maneuver through either the Basic Attack Maneuver
  or Signature Technique Maneuver. That declared Attacking Maneuver gains an Energy
  Charge. Each time you would use the Energy Charge Maneuver after declaring an
  Attacking Maneuver but before using the declared Attacking Maneuver, any use of
  the Energy Charge Maneuver instead only grants an additional Energy Charge to the
  originally declared Attacking Maneuver.

  Until you use the chosen Attacking Maneuver, you suffer from the Guard Down
  Combat Condition and you cannot use any other Attacking Maneuver or Standard
  Maneuver.

---

# No script, and not for want of one.
#
# What this Maneuver does is declare something and then keep adding to it across
# later uses, and a script runs once and is done. So `charge: true` in the header
# hands it to the code that can hold a declaration open - the same way `surge` and
# `defend` are handled - and what it does is written there rather than here.
#
# What it comes to:
#   - the first use asks which Attacking Maneuver is being charged and with which
#     Profile, and gives it one Energy Charge. The Profile is part of the declaration:
#     when the attack is finally thrown it is made with that Profile and no other,
#     which is what makes this a declaration rather than a reminder
#   - every use after that gives that same Maneuver another, up to seven
#   - Guard Down lasts as long as the charging does
#   - no other Attacking or Standard Maneuver may be used meanwhile - this one and
#     the declared attack are the two exceptions, both named by the rule
#   - each charge adds 1d6(T) to the attack's Wound Roll, or 1d8(T) if the Maneuver
#     carries the `signature` tag
